. Basically only three facts need to be established by  the claimants for assessing compensation in the case of  death :-
 (a) age of the deceased; (b) income of the deceased;
 and the (c) the number of dependents.

The issues to  be determined by the Tribunal to arrive at the loss of  dependency are (i) additions/deductions to be made for Rama Devi (Dar) vs Balbir Singh(269/20Dfc) on 6 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/34293009/
5  arriving at the income; (ii) the deduction to be made  towards the personal living expenses of the deceased;
 and (iii) the multiplier to be applied with reference of  the age of the deceased.
